      'His own lines are quoted only where the recording reads cleanly; the rest is given as summary. Three details of his evidence are corrected from the record: the Pied Piper legend comes from Hamelin in Germany, not London; Franz Mesmer was a German physician educated by Jesuits whose theory was animal magnetism, not a rabbi who devised hypnotic beats; and the ownership of the music industry is held by corporations, not by a handful of named people. His critique of celebrity teaching is kept where it concerns public messages (a book’s dating counsel, an album that paired worship and sensual songs, a film franchise’s portrait of church people); his remarks about the private lives of named living people are left out, because the Word forbids passing on what cannot be established. The teaching that lucifer led heaven’s music is drawn from Ezekiel 28:13, which mentions tabrets and pipes in the covering cherub’s creation; the office he assigns goes beyond the verse.',
