      'His own lines are quoted only where the recording reads cleanly; the rest is given as summary. In this sermon he read aloud from published material about the Illuminati, Karl Marx, Manly P. Hall and the dollar’s seal; the lesson gives the record on each instead of repeating the claims: the Illuminati was founded a year after the Revolutionary War began; Marx was born to a family that had converted and was baptized Lutheran, and no record shows the memberships attributed to him; the seal’s designers were, with one exception whose ideas were not used, not Masons. His statement that the White House had called Sandy Hook a drill is false; 26 people, 20 of them first-graders, were murdered, and the hoax was later found defamatory in court. His other claims of staged events, camps and poisoned water, and his remarks about a named living person, are left out because the record does not support them. His teaching on Genesis 6, hybrid creatures and dinosaurs goes beyond the text; the Word names the giants and stops. His critique of the seven-mountain teaching is given as his reading of John 18:36.',
